# Rat cradle for the count-rate runs (setup q86rat of NECR_main_std.mac). It does not move in this test: all
# 10 parts are placed at (0, {cradleY}, 0), with cradleY from the SETUP block of NECR_main_std.mac.
# The cradle shape was taken from the 511 keV attenuation map (mu-map) of the Quad86 coil with the rat cradle,
# turned into STL surfaces and imported as tessellated volumes at real size (stl80/bed_s0087,
# stl/bed_s0088 ... bed_s0095, stl80/bed_s0096). Axial details shorter than 2 mm were averaged.
# Material Bed_HDPE (polyethylene C2H4, 0.95 g/cm3, coil_bed_real/Coil3Bed.db). The STL names keep the mu-map
# value Plastic_0744 (AC_Plastic_0744, 0.80 g/cm3), but that value is lower than the attenuation of any solid
# plastic. The real mouse and rat cradles are made of the same white, opaque plastic, which I modelled as
# polyethylene. The wall thicknesses agree with my caliper measurements.
# With cradleY = 12.240 mm the centred phantom rests on the cradle with a 0.01 mm gap; the cradle reaches
# r 36.16 mm (Quad86 inner tube from r 43.0 mm).
# Cut at z = -80 ... +80 mm (beyond the detectors) to save time. The parts (ratbed_s00NN) are attached to the
# PhantomSD; necr_analysis.py counts scatter in them as 'object' scatter.

/gate/world/daughters/name ratbed_s0087
/gate/world/daughters/insert tessellated
/gate/ratbed_s0087/geometry/setPathToSTLFile coil_bed_real/stl80/bed_s0087_Plastic_0744.stl
/gate/ratbed_s0087/setMaterial Bed_HDPE
/gate/ratbed_s0087/placement/setTranslation 0 {cradleY} 0 mm
/gate/ratbed_s0087/vis/setColor white
/gate/ratbed_s0087/attachPhantomSD

/gate/world/daughters/name ratbed_s0088
/gate/world/daughters/insert tessellated
/gate/ratbed_s0088/geometry/setPathToSTLFile coil_bed_real/stl/bed_s0088_Plastic_0744.stl
/gate/ratbed_s0088/setMaterial Bed_HDPE
/gate/ratbed_s0088/placement/setTranslation 0 {cradleY} 0 mm
/gate/ratbed_s0088/vis/setColor white
/gate/ratbed_s0088/attachPhantomSD

